> >   #mount -a
> > the system prompts error:
> >   msfs_mount: The mount device does not match the linked device.
> >       check linked device in /etc/fdmns/domain
> >   msfs_mount: setting root device name to root_device RW
> >
> > The contents in /etc/fdmns/ and /etc/fstab are the same as the source
> > disk, but the root file system mounted is different: in the source
> > disk, it's root_domain; but in the target disk, it's root_device.
> > Following is the output of df when booted with the target disk:
> >   #df
> >   file system                 mounted on
> >   root_device                 /
> >   /proc                       /proc
> >   user_domain#usr             /usr
> >   var_domain#var              /var
> >   home_domain#home            /home
> >
> > where, root_device should be root_domain#root.
> >
> > Can somebody tell me what the wrong with the system? and is there
> > another way to duplicate system disk? All filesystems are created with
> > Tru64Unix v5.1 AdvFS.
> >
> > Thanks in advance!


To duplicate the system disk.

Format the disk first by (assuming this is not advfs) 

disklabel -t nfs -wr dsk1 rz1ed

Then
# mount /dev/dsk1a /mnt
# dump -0 -f - / | (cd /mnt; restore -x -f -)
# umount /mnt
# mount /dev/dsk1g /mnt
# dump -0 -f - /usr | (cd /mnt; restore -x -f -)
# umount /mnt
...
and so on.

