OK so you managed to boot to single user mode. This means you have
succeeded in copying the disk. However the new disk is more than
likeley called /dev/disk/dsk2c not /dev/disk/dsk0c.

Boot from the cd, mount the destination disk, change the pointer
in /etc/fdmns/root_domain  to point to the correct place. (change
rz0 to rz2)

Reboot.
This should be enough.
HTH
Adam





