Steve,

  The 6 step process as drummed into me is as follows :-

1. Remove the failed disk from the disk group retaining the media
records thus

# voldg �g mydg �k rmdisk media_name

2. Remove the disk access record

# voldisk rm disk_access_name

3. Restore the disklabel

   #disklabel �wr rz?? disktype
    (assuming no copy of the label was saved)

   #disklabel �r �R rz?? /saved_label disktype
     (if the label was saved)

4. Initialise the new disk for use with LSM

   # voldisksetup �i rz?? nconfig=? nlogs=? privlength=??
     (assuming no copy of the label was saved)

   # voldisk �f init rz?? offset=16
      (if the label was saved)


5. Associate the new disk to a disk media record/disk group

# voldg �g mydg �k adddisk media_name=disk_access_name

6. Recover(synchronise) the plexes in the diskgroup

# volrecover �g mydg -sb


There are shorter ways, but the trainer was right. "This will always
work, other methods you're on yer own..."

Cheers

Gary


