To copy system disk dsk0 to dsk1 and make dsk1 the new system disk

disklabel -z dsk1 (output disk must not be labeled)

dd -if= /dev/rdisk/dsk0c of=/dev/rdisk/dsk1c bs=64k

Change the links from dsk0 to dsk1

cd /etc/fdmns

These are symbolic links
root_domain
usr_domain
var_domain
anyother_domains

Remove the symbolic links to dsk0
rm /etc/fdmns/root_domain/dsk0a
rm /etc/fdmns/usr_domain/dsk0g
rm /etc/fdmns/var_domain/dsk0h

Make new symbolic links to dsk1
ln -s /dev/dsk/dsk1a /etc/fdmns/root_domain/dsk1a

repeat this for usr and var and any other advfs domains you may have on dsk0

vi /etc/sysconfigtab

search for vm: and change the swapdevice to dsk1b

reboot your system

Regards
Peter Barone



