>I'm running a mixture of Tru64 and Linux, with a Tru64 central logging
>host. The Tru64 syslogd does not understand authpriv messages, and drops
>them. I was wondering if there was a way to send all authpriv as auth
>from the linux boxes, or to log all unknown types to a certain file. 
>Thanks
>-Lucas

Do you have the local0 through local7 facilities activated in addition to the
kern, user, mail, etc, facilities in /etc/syslog.conf?  Here's why:  I have a
Sonicwall firewall which claimed that it could send syslog messages to a
syslogd server but no messages showed up in any of my existing logs.  Then, in
an experiment, I activated local0 through local7 and lo and behold, firewall
messages started showing up in the local0 facility log file.   This might be a
similar situation with your authpriv messages.  Hope this helps.

