On 12 Apr 2002 10:48:58 GMT, SpitsOnSpammers wrote:

> Can anyone tell me if the syslog messages that a syslogd daemon accepts
> and writes to a log are just simple character strings?

Yes.  Yes.

If you run syslogd in debug mode (-d) the syslog-er will not daemonize
and will print the incoming message to the screen as well as to the
regular targets.  There you'll see as well as the actual message, the
facility/priority code sent with it (so the syslogger "knows" which
targets to send that message to).

I hope that helps...

