I do not know if there is an explanation for this, but I have seen
more than one system with such 'ld' behaviour ... I think Irix ld
does this as well.

Presumably 'ld' designers thought the "half-cooked" ld output
is good for something. It probably *is* good for debugging 'ld'
itself ...

The Makefile workarounds I have often encountered:

  $(EXE): $(OBJS)
        $(CC) $(CFLAGS) -o $@ $(OBJS) $(LIBS) || $(RM) $@

or

  $(EXE): $(OBJS)
        $(CC) $(CFLAGS) -o tmp.$@ $(OBJS) $(LIBS) && $(MV) tmp.$@ $@

Cheers,


