In article <6445524b.0204150450.4964cec1@posting.google.com> dub@latnet.lv (Dub) writes:
>This is a very stupid question, but please tell me how to find out
>which version is running on a Tru64 host.
>'uname' does not print last letter.
>
>uname -a
>OSF1 ivr1 V4.0 1229 alpha

sizer -v will give you the exact version string:

# sizer -v
Digital UNIX V4.0G (Rev. 1530); Fri Nov 30 10:45:04 EST 2001


Also, for *far*  more detail than you probably want, you can look
in /usr/sys/conf, at the "version.*" files. Major.Minor.Variant
has the set:

# cat version.major version.minor version.variant
4
0
G

Lastly, the top line of /etc/motd has a copy of the sizer -v string.

