I just downloaded and built Dante v1.1.12-pre1 and in very limited testing
it seems to work.
I'm using Tru64 UNIX V5.1.

I defined these environment variables before running configure:

CC=cc
MAKE=/usr/local/bin/make
INSTALL=/usr/bin/installbsd
AWK=/usr/bin/awk
NM=/usr/bin/nm


I edited configure to remove "-oldc" from comp_flags in the alpha*-dec-osf*
case.

You need gnu make (I have it as /usr/local/bin/make ; change your MAKE env
var as requred)
I believe you also need bison (e.g., /usr/local/bin/bison).

Then I just ran ./configure and then $MAKE and it built without errors, just
a few Warnings about function pointer prototypes.

My test system only has one NIC so the internal and external addresses are
the same in sockd.conf, and my authentication method is "none".   I
configured Netscape Communicator to use it as SOCKS proxy, and I can confirm
the connections in /var/adm/syslog.dated/current/daemon.log :


