Good luck to you. Your posts work. :-)

Do you want to restric account only or do you like to restrict to
specific IP address. 
If you like restriction by IP or domain name you use tcpd. Instal it
than correct '/etc/inetd.conf' like this:
ftp     stream  tcp     nowait  root    /usr/sbin/tcpd          ftpd
Then in files '/etc/hosts.allow' write IPs or domain names you like and
in '/etc/hosts.deny' write ALL:ALL:.

Restriction to specific IP address or domain name is possible directly
in Tru64 like above, but I think that restriction to specific username
and directory is possible onlly in ftp server software or you can create
user account "ftpuser" on your comp in a group let say "ftpgroup" that
has no permissions in your personal group. This way you can open all
your directories to your personal group but target directory is only
open to ftp user account.

I hope some of this helps.

