Actually Tru64 UNIX is only a 2.5+ Mach kernel with a BSD UNIX on top, 
and various technologies added from the OSF/1 consoursium.  As far as I 
know, the only Mach 3.0 kernel UNIX is Mac OS X.  Mach is running under 
a FreeBSD UNIX.  Apple calls this combo Darwin and the sources can be 
downloaded from Apple <www.apple.com/darwin>.  The Apple GUI called 
Aqua, is what you have to pay money for and requires a Macintosh 
computer to run it, also from Apple.

I wouldn't call HP-UX messed up, but rather coming from a different 
origin.  A lot of the freeware software comes from BSD derived systems 
(even Linux has stronger BSD leanings), but HP-UX has its roots in AT&T 
System V (I think), so some of the ways of doing things are different.

