Erkki Aalto wrote:

> Does anyone know, which SIA call resets the u_numunsuclog counter?
> Sia_ses_authent seems to increment it if the password is wrong,
> but it does not reset it when the password is right.

There are 2 counters - one the count of unsuccessful logins since the last time I
told you(u_flogins) and the other the number of consecutive unsuccessful
logins(u_numunsuclog).

When you have a successful login, the sia_ses_launch() routine will call a
routine that will "clear" the u_numunsuclog value.  When you have a successful
login with a tty to display the number of unsuccessful logins since we last told
you, then the u_flogins is cleared.


